name "sec:Reinforcement-learning"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Reinforcement learning is a subfield of machine learning, in which an agent
 autonomously learns a strategy for an environment in order to maximize
 cumulative reward.
 RL problems, unlike supervised learning, require a sequential decision
 process for which the agent must develop a policy.
 At each time step, the environment is in a state s, which the agent can
 observe and decide for an available action, which will lead to a succeeding
 state s' and a reward, as can be seen in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:RL-basics"

\end_inset

.
 The probability to reach state s' is assumed to only depend on the current
 state s, which formalizes a 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
emph{Markov Decision Process}
\end_layout

\end_inset

 (MDP).
 If the current state of the system cannot be derived from the available
 observations, the MDP is only partially observable.
 
\end_layout

