\begin_layout Subsection
Tree Construction
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Despite their genetic representation, genes cannot be randomly mixed.
 Trees must be evaluable, which is also known as the concept of 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
emph{closure}
\end_layout

\end_inset

 and requires a strategy for dealing with type conversion and handling of
 invalid expressions.
 A conversion between Boolean and numeric values should be strongly typed,
 as this produces more natural mathematical compositions than automatic
 conversion 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Strongly_typed_GP"
literal "true"

\end_inset

.
 This requires explicit type conversion, e.g.
 with comparison operators or If-operators, as well as mutually exclusive
 crossover evolution to ensure closure.
 Type-correct expressions can still be mathematically invalid, which is
 difficult to prevent.
 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

For frequently occurring problems, such as the 
\backslash
emph{division by zero}, a dummy value is returned ($
\backslash
frac{x}{0}
\backslash
rightarrow 1$).
\end_layout

\end_inset

 However, to avoid changing the essence of other operators too much, faulty
 trees are mostly discarded and replaced randomly.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Finding new genes requires the construction of random trees and branches,
 for which the 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
emph{full} and 
\backslash
emph{grow}
\end_layout

\end_inset

 method are available.
 Both methods build append nodes to a certain depth, but the 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
emph{full}
\end_layout

\end_inset

 method allows terminal nodes only at the lowest level while the grow method
 also allows terminal nodes to be inserted by chance (50%).
 The full method has a much higher branching factor and creates more complex
 formulae than the grow method.
 This affects the tree structure and thus the formula, as can be seen in
 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:grow-vs-full-method"

\end_inset

.
 Since neither is clearly preferable, a 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
emph{ramped half-n-half}
\end_layout

\end_inset

 combination of both methods is proposed 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "gp-half-ramped"
literal "true"

\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The tree depth and the number of tree nodes are capped to prevent a complexity
 bloat.
 Since the performance gain decreases with increasing complexity, the number
 of nodes can be used as second objective to create a Pareto front, which
 provides the ability to trade off complexity and fitness between candidates
 rather than just saving the fittest candidate.
\end_layout

