\begin_layout Section
Related Work
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Related-Work"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Industrial control strategies feature many peculiarities which can now be
 addressed with reinforcement learning, such as high dimensionality 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "siemens-gas-turbine-rl-nn"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 or high stochasticity 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "PSONN_fuzzy_RL_Hein_Udluft,siemens-rl-stochastic-bayesian-nn"
literal "true"

\end_inset

, which are not interpretable.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Despite much interest, only little work covers the problems of finding interpret
able policies.
 In 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Hein_Udluft_Runkler_interpretable_gp"
literal "true"

\end_inset

, Hein et al.
 present a method which uses genetic programming to create holistically
 interpretable policies for industrial controllers.
 In 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "hein_fuzzy_gp"
literal "true"

\end_inset

, the possibility of deriving a fuzzy rule set for more complex problems
 is presented.
 More secure offline training on a surrogate model, such as by performing
 a symbolic regression on previously collected transition samples, is evaluated
 in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "daniel_hein_doktorarbeit"
literal "true"

\end_inset

.
 Despite their simplicity, the generated formulas are often hardly comprehensibl
e because they are too mathematical and contain no recognizable intuition.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Tresp_prior_knowledge"
literal "true"

\end_inset

, it is shown how prior knowledge in the form of a set of rules can be used
 to pre-structure policies that provide improved trustworthiness and allow
 a probabilistic interpretation.
 A similar method is evaluated in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "residual-dynamic-learning"
literal "true"

\end_inset

, where human control strategies in an industrial area are enhanced with
 machine learning.
 These approaches allow a stochastic version of interpretability, but not
 in a global manner such that novelties can be easily recognized.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
FloatBarrier
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Chapter
Familiar Genetic Programming 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "chap:Familiar-Genetic-Programming"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In the following, the implementation of the approach to enhance genetic
 programming with familiarity is presented.
 The approach requires an expert program and transition samples of a better
 black box, the concept can be seen in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "img:plausibility-concept"

\end_inset

.
 The paradigm of familiarity is introduced in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sec:Familiarity"

\end_inset

 and potential and expected benefits are discussed.
 In order to protect familiar structures, the 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
emph{Tree Edit Distance} (TED)
\end_layout

\end_inset

 is presented as complexity measure to calculate the amount of required
 changes to the origin tree in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "sec:Familiarity-Measurement-TED"

\end_inset

.
 For further protection, 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "subsec:Fixed-nodes"

\end_inset

 introduces the fixed core as extension of the TED.
 Particular features of the GP suite are described in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "sec:GP-Suite-Implementation"

\end_inset

.
 Lastly, a tree unification algorithm is presented in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "sec:sympy-tree-reduction"

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

