\begin_layout Section
Industrial Benchmark 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Industrial-benchmark"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The industrial benchmark was introduced by scientists at Siemens to meet
 the high requirements of complex, real world industrial processes 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "industrialBenchmark"
literal "true"

\end_inset

.
 The state space is high-dimensional and only partially observable (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "IB-observations-state"

\end_inset

), so that the development of the observations must be taken into account
 in the form of a retrospective observation.
 The reward depends on a combination of actions 0 and 1, as well as action
 2, which strongly punishes misbehavior.
 Finally, high stochastic system dynamics further complicates learning reliable
 policies.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
No good human-developed control strategies for the IB are known; the best
 available strategy is doing 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

nothing
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

, which is also considered to be respectably good.
 
\end_layout

