\begin_layout Paragraph
Black box: PSONN
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As black box technology, a 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
emph{particle swarm optimisation neural networks} (PSONN)
\end_layout

\end_inset

 agent with a calculated IB reward of 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$5353$
\end_layout

\end_inset

 was chosen 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "PSONN_fuzzy_RL_Hein_Udluft"
literal "true"

\end_inset

.
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The initial states of the IB in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "daniel_hein_doktorarbeit"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 were randomized.
 Comparable values could be obtained by a randomized initial state, but
 the results were very volatile.
 The difference of agents in Hein's work was 7% worse on average, which
 was used for comparison.
 For the PSONN policy, this results in a adjusted penalty value of 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$5728/1.07=5353$
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\end_inset

 Particle swarm optimization algorithms, similar to GP, can find solutions
 for many types of problems.
 The solution space is populated by a swarm population, which should find
 the best optima by swarm intelligence.
 This method is very interesting as a black box, because the model is very
 sparse and might be difficult to fit with symbolic regression.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Offline Data Selection
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Offline-Data-Selection"

\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The data for the symbolic regression are generated online, on the benchmark,
 using the appropriate black box approach and all observable states and
 the associated actions are saved (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "tab:The-generated-data"

\end_inset

).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When the priority is to improve performance, data selection is conceivable,
 but stochasticity or long-term strategies are often difficult to distinguish
 from actual misbehavior.
 Clustering for unknown state combinations in the black box data was also
 discarded to guarantee balanced and authentic results.
\end_layout

