\begin_layout Chapter
Results 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "chap:Results"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this section, six familiarity-based GP runs are evaluated and compared
 with regular runs in more detail.
 All runs were trained with the parameters described in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "sec:GP-Suite-Implementation"

\end_inset

.
 To minimize the possible unfair influence of evolution, a population of
 1000 individuals was chosen, trained comparatively long over 4000 generations.
 A total of 90 different expressions were tested, from which only the most
 important are presented below.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Pareto candidates found are primarily examined for familiarity and interpret
ability.
 Their performance is compared both in terms of regression error and real
 performance, but also examined for implications for safety.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Mountain Car
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Three approaches are analyzed in this benchmark.
 The first is simple and safe, fetching maximum momentum, the second is
 a more complex parabolic formula, and the third is a nested If-distinction
 for which the reversal points have been manually optimized.
 Furthermore, fixed core structures and obligatory acceleration were tested.
 The latter means that action 1 cannot be selected in these runs, so that
 the regression error cannot decrease to 0 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

($0.023$ for SARSA-200, $0.066$ for SARSA-75)
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
 
\end_layout

