\begin_layout Subsection
Regular GP Results
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Regular GP runs could completely solve the problem from complexity 18 upwards.
 Altering solution strategies are noticeable in the medium-complex candidate
 range (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:mtc200-mse-scratch-pareto"

\end_inset

).
 Candidates do not try to distinguish between action 0 and 1, but provide
 a continuous and often fluctuating mathematical mapping between inputs
 and outputs (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:MC-scratch-3examples"

\end_inset

).
 Simple agents perform poorly on the real benchmark and could not exceed
 the maximum-momentum strategy, for example the three-noded formula 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$
\backslash
ensuremath{
\backslash
text{vel}^{-5.0}}$
\end_layout

\end_inset

