\begin_layout Section
Discussion
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For both benchmarks, extensions were found for all expert strategies, whereby
 known structures were clearly intact.
 Compared to regular GP results, no major negative effects on the regression
 error were observed.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The benefits of familiarity for interpretability are difficult to quantify,
 as a very simple mathematical formula can be much more difficult to understand
 than a comprehensive strategy that is intuitive.
 The main advantage is, that by preserving the core of a tree, the central
 idea is adopted as well, which has very likely a structuring purpose.
 Regular GP metrics drive a population to a functional, holistic and easy
 to evolve tree architecture.
 The contradiction between interpretability and complexity becomes clear
 with the If-operator.
 With 3 inputs, it has the largest branching factor among all operators,
 which leads to node-rich and complex trees.
 On the other side, it improves interpretability like no other operator,
 as each child branch can be interpreted as a separate chunk.
 Since an equivalent effect can also be achieved with less complex formulas
 (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:if-operator-composition"

\end_inset

), it rarely occurs in regular GP candidates.
 
\end_layout

